What tam-pane is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-27, with W43


STATE

  Version 0.2.17 on dev (W43) adds the Tamlinux 0.7.x Stage 2 (Milestones
  13 & 14) compositor primitives: logical monitor enable/disable with window
  displacement and reclamation (`dispatch monitor enable|disable`,
  `tp.dsp.monitor("enable"|"disable", ...)`, `enabled=<0|1>` on `monitors`),
  connected input device listing (`devices` IPC, allowed while locked),
  window pinning and `0xID`-targeted window dispatches (`close`, `float`,
  `pin`, `resize_exact`, `move_exact`, `center`, `raise`, plus `tp.dsp.pin`,
  `tp.dsp.center`, `tp.dsp.raise`, and `pinned=<0|1>` on `windows`/`focused`),
  and themeable focused/unfocused window border colors (`border_color_focused`,
  `border_color_unfocused` in `tp.config`, live-updated on reload).
  All native unit suites (`test_lua` 650, `test_ipc` 215, `test_gamma` 1235,
  etc.) and headless input tests (977 checks) pass with zero `libxcb` NEEDED.

  Version 0.2.16 on dev (W42) adds the Tamlinux 0.7.x Phase 2 (Milestones
  11 & 12) compositor primitives: `lock_state` IPC query, `session.lock` /
  `session.unlock` events (IPC and Lua), DPMS-while-locked, native color
  temperature / gamma LUTs (`src/gamma_math.c`, `src/gamma.c`, `gamma`
  query, `dispatch gamma <1000..25000|reset|off>`, `tp.dsp.gamma`,
  `gamma.change` event), and native screen freeze + pixel sampling
  (`src/capture.c`, `TP_LAYER_FREEZE`, `freeze` query, `dispatch freeze
  on|off`, `tp.dsp.freeze`, `pixel [x y]` query gated while locked).
  All native unit suites (including `test_gamma`, 1235 checks) and headless
  input tests (913 checks) pass with zero `libxcb` NEEDED.

  Version 0.2.15 on dev (W41) adds a pointer-focus setting, cross-display
  tiled drag, checked key dispatch for macros, and window-change events.
  Headless input passes. The physical Tamlinux trial awaits Test.

  Version 0.2.14 on dev (W40) adds `dispatch monitor mode <output>
  <W>x<H>[@<Hz>]`, which replies OK only when the mode commit went
